@page "/mudblazor"

<PageTitle>Fitting MudBlazor</PageTitle>

<h1>Fitting MudBlazor</h1>
<p>Formidable supports MudBlazor. The sample's page puts two MudBlazor controls (a text field and a select) inside <code>FormidableField</code>, one per field. Each control takes the field's id, state class and aria attributes through one <code>@@attributes</code> splat, and Formidable's messages show under it.</p>
<p>The page with the working form runs when you download the sample and run it locally. This live demo leaves it out so the sample stays focused on Formidable. Loading MudBlazor here would add about 300 KB to every visitor's first load. Loading it only when this page opens would need extra loading code, which has nothing to do with what the sample teaches.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/xfunc-pty-ltd/formidable/blob/main/samples/Formidable.Sample/Pages/MudBlazorFitting.razor">Read the page's source on GitHub</a>, or follow the README's steps to <a href="https://github.com/xfunc-pty-ltd/formidable#run-the-sample-locally">run the sample locally</a>.</p>
